## Slidev slide authoring rules

- **Slide boundaries**: use `---` on its own line to separate slides.
- **Frontmatter**:
  - Use YAML frontmatter at the top of a slide file as needed (theme, title, transition, layout, etc.).
  - Keep frontmatter minimal and consistent; prefer repo defaults unless a slide truly needs overrides.
- **Layouts**:
  - Prefer built-in layouts (`center`, `two-cols`, `image-right`, etc.) before custom CSS.
  - When using `two-cols`, keep content balanced and readable at typical projector resolutions.
- **Animations / interactivity**:
  - Prefer progressive disclosure (`v-click`, `v-after`) over dense walls of text.
  - Use `v-motion` sparingly; avoid distracting motion that hurts comprehension.
- **Notes**:
  - Put presenter notes in the **last HTML comment block** of a slide.
  - Notes should include speaking points and timing cues for workshops.
- **Code blocks**:
  - Prefer small, focused snippets; highlight relevant lines.
  - If code is reused, store it under `snippets/` and import it instead of duplicating.
- **External snippet import**:
  - Use `<<< @/snippets/<file>#snippet` (with a `#region snippet` in the snippet file).
- **Diagrams**:
  - Use Mermaid/PlantUML where it improves clarity; keep diagrams readable and not overly complex.
- **Accessibility**:
  - Provide `alt` text for images.
  - Avoid relying solely on color to convey meaning.

